    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "In this repro, the function `foo()` is mutating a tensor with overlapping data. This is undefined behavior ([docs](https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/stable/generated/torch.as_strided.html)), because there is a data race to perform the mutation, so you can get different results depending on the kernel that runs, and we end up with a different behavior under eager vs compile.\n\nI think it would be reasonable though for us to try to detect and error on this case under compile though, which is better than \"different results than eager\".",
