    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "@bdhirsh , I tried the same repro from above and here is my observation on the difference between compile and eager. \n\nIn eager: The overlapping is happening with [0,1] and [1,0]. The in-place add 1 twice at the overlapping. So we see that element to be +2 from the actual value. For example if as_strided gives me [[-2,-1],[-1,2]]. The output will be [[-1,1],[1,2]]\n\nIn compile: The addition is happening only once so I am getting [[-1,0],[0,2]]. \n\nShould we do addition in the overlapping twice or there should be error on this case? \n\nI would like to move forward implementing with your suggestion on the same.",
